cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use projmem in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "projmem: drift-aware code memory for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  projmem is a structured-memory tool for AI-assisted code work. It
  stores agent conclusions about code as verifiable claims, re-checks
  each claim against the current codebase, and reports exactly which
  beliefs became false after a code change — rather than opaque
  "confidence decayed" signals.
authors:
  - name: "projmem contributors"
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-04-18"
keywords:
  - "static analysis"
  - "code understanding"
  - "llm-agents"
  - "drift detection"
  - "tree-sitter"
  - "ai agent memory"
